Real GCC-backend support for #[rustc_cxx_throws], catch-all AND
typed (P09.62-gcc / P09.64-gcc / P09.68-gcc all closed):

- cxx_catch_landing_pad (master feature): set the personality the
  SSA layer picked (__gxx_personality_v0 for typed catches), read
  the in-flight exception via __builtin_eh_pointer(0), and compute
  the selector. gccjit has no llvm.eh.typeid.for, so typed selection
  calls the cxx runtime's __rustcc_cxx_match_typeinfo(exn, tis, n)
  over a per-pad static array of the clause _ZTI addresses — it
  returns the same 1-based index LLVM's typeid translation yields,
  feeding the unchanged __rustcc_cxx_catch_typed contract. Args are
  cast to the matcher's own param types (it may be declared from its
  Rust definition in the same CGU with different nominal pointers).
- context: real cxx_throws_catch_fn / cxx_throws_catch_typed_fn
  (CxxRawError {i32, char*} by-value returns; address + fn-ptr type
  so call() routes via function_ptr_call), cxx_typeinfo_global
  (imported _ZTI), cxx_typeinfo_personality (__gxx_personality_v0).
- function_ptr_call: when the SSA-provided fn type disagrees with
  the value's declared type (param count), the SSA type wins — the
  throws wrap changes a foreign fn's call ABI (sret CxxRawError)
  while its decl keeps the source signature; LLVM's opaque pointers
  hid this, gccjit's typed pointers ICEd
  (new_call_through_ptr: got 1 args, expected 2).

Probes (container, pure-GCC pipeline, LLVM controls identical):
- cxx_throws_native: ok=10, Err(Unknown), phase-2 passed
- typed smoke: ok=10, Err(Domain), Err(Range) — both clause matches
- subclass demo + class smoke re-verified on both backends
